\name{cellucid_history_step_delete}
\alias{cellucid_history_step_delete}
\title{Delete a step}
\usage{
cellucid_history_step_delete(viewer, step)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{step}{A step of the tracker in use, by its id (history_get lists the steps). Text. Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{flagged} (Steps that no longer apply), \code{head} (The step shown now), \code{journal} (Its Recently deleted entry), \code{reapplied} (Steps applied again).
}
\description{
Move one step to Recently deleted; only the later steps that changed or read what it changed are applied again, and one that no longer applies is kept, flagged.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.step.delete} (History). It moves the viewer's history, as the person's Undo, Redo or a click on a step does: it makes no step of the history.

When an agent (Claude, ChatGPT) runs it, the viewer asks the person first (deletes-saved); from R it is not asked.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_step_delete(viewer, step = "s3")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
